		{
			"id": "113358356095412344",
			"parentId": "113358298455212580",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@jakelazaroff/113358355570823579",
			"author": {
				"name": "jake lazaroff",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@jakelazaroff",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/829/533/556/740/279/original/69a92e79689324bc.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-10-23T19:20:36.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://ruby.social/@konnorrogers\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>konnorrogers</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> which? i mostly work with react (using CSS modules) and svelte, and neither of those will generate inline styles unless you explicitly set style attributes. AFAIK that’s pretty normal, so i’m also curious where that markup came from!</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "113358365860497433",
			"parentId": "113358356095412344",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/113358365860497433",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-10-23T19:23:13.135Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@jakelazaroff\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>jakelazaroff</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://ruby.social/@konnorrogers\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>konnorrogers</span></a></span> it’s from bluesky</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "113358383498798253",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@khalidabuhakmeh/113358383446491751",
			"author": {
				"name": "Khalid ⚡",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@khalidabuhakmeh",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/296/176/354/255/607/original/70d4899634530145.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-10-23T19:27:41.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I think I might have an idea. Are there any hints to what the backend tech is?</p><p>I’ve seen this technique used on the <a href=\"https://mastodon.social/tags/dotnet\" class=\"mention hashtag\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">#<span>dotnet</span></a> side of things with Blazor, where each component is given a class as an identifier so that downstream components can be targeted when the UI is mutated.</p><p>The inline CSS could be additional scoped styles for changes from the defaults.</p><p>This is a guess based on the screenshot.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "113358387123089104",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://hachyderm.io/@olets/113358387089768481",
			"author": {
				"name": "Henry Bley-Vroman",
				"url": "https://hachyderm.io/@olets",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/110/811/441/260/746/867/original/e2f49b9726cb0b97.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2024-10-23T19:28:37.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Could be Tailwind/Windi/Uno/etc. They determine which classes to build by scanning the source code. For styles that are dynamic *and* not from a set known in advance, you have to use some other solution - like inline `style`.</p><p>Can imagine that forcing the `style=\"background-color:…\"`.</p><p>Harder to see it forcing `style=\"flex-direction… gap… padding\"` (sounds like known variant, typically pseudocoded `class={condition ? 'flex-direction-… gap-… padding-…')}` - cf <a href=\"https://tailwindcss.com/docs/content-configuration#dynamic-class-names\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">tailwindcss.com/docs/content-c</span><span class=\"invisible\">onfiguration#dynamic-class-names</span></a>)</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "113358388617692391",
			"parentId": "113358284447852403",
			"url": "https://fosstodon.org/@mahryekuh/113358388493553920",
			"author": {
