			},
			"date": "2024-10-23T19:28:58.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Boosting it so others can suffer through it too. Call it early Halloween. 😈🎃</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "113358398401437642",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://social.lol/@ryan/113358398371856438",
			"author": {
				"name": "ryan",
				"url": "https://social.lol/@ryan",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-10-23T19:31:29.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> The class structure kind of looks like the output of Emotion? <a href=\"https://emotion.sh/docs/introduction\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"\">emotion.sh/docs/introduction</span><span class=\"invisible\"></span></a></p><p>But I think even that library wouldn’t normally use inline styles, may be a dev decision or it’s like a component library also in play 😬</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
